From: vyos-mox <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: reserve the TF-A memory region on the Turris Mox

The device tree that U-Boot passes to Linux on the Turris Mox has no
reserved-memory node for the Trusted Firmware-A region at 64 MiB (BL31 sits at
0x4023000). Linux hands the memory to the page allocator and overwrites the PSCI
firmware, so later PSCI calls (SYSTEM_RESET, CPU_OFF) hang the system. Reserve the
2 MiB psci-area@4000000 of armada-37xx.dtsi for cznic,turris-mox when the device
tree does not.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/mm/init.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/mm/init.c
@@ -287,6 +287,18 @@ void __init arm64_memblock_init(void)
 	}
 
 	early_init_fdt_scan_reserved_mem();
+
+	/*
+	 * The device tree U-Boot passes on the Turris Mox lacks the reserved-memory
+	 * node for the TF-A (BL31) region at 64 MiB, so Linux hands that memory to
+	 * the allocator, overwrites the PSCI firmware, and from then on PSCI calls
+	 * such as SYSTEM_RESET and CPU_OFF hang the system. Reserve it here, as
+	 * psci-area@4000000 in armada-37xx.dtsi does.
+	 */
+	if (of_flat_dt_is_compatible(of_get_flat_dt_root(), "cznic,turris-mox")) {
+		memblock_reserve(0x4000000, 0x200000);
+		memblock_mark_nomap(0x4000000, 0x200000);
+	}
 }
 
 void __init bootmem_init(void)
